{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"1f013f6426b27f8cb555c22229b6c039f0c3bf25e128f377b49ae37cdbaeeacb","digest":{"component_or_area":"Jira reconcile bridge — outbound comment sync","key_entities":["comment_ids","RECONCILER_MARKER","outbound_comments._normalize_comment_body","_decorate_outbound_comment","_TRUNCATION_SUFFIX","REB-1861","REB-1580","REB-1829","adapters/jira/comment_limits.py","bd80-0603-7d44-4d9f","irongrey-chubby-oxpecker","accountId 712020:6471376f-4e5e-4ed2-8c05-330827bc387e","GitHub Actions run 32403944666",".github/workflows/reconcile-bridge.yml"],"problem_keywords":["duplicate comments","jira","comment dedup","reconcile bridge","data cleanup","bot-authored duplicates"],"propositions":["The Jira reconcile bridge re-posted identical comments on every hourly pass because the PRIMARY comment-id dedup map (comment_ids) was inert/empty, causing REB-1861 to reach and stick at Jira's 5000-comment hard cap and blocking new comment ingestion.","29,931 duplicate bot-authored comments authored by accountId 712020:6471376f-4e5e-4ed2-8c05-330827bc387e were deleted across 27 of 30 affected issues using a keep-oldest-per-distinct-normalized-body rule, with full pre-deletion backups and independent post-deletion verification confirming zero lost distinct bodies and zero touched non-candidate comments.","REB-1861 reduced from 5000 comments to 79; REB-1580, REB-1829, and REB-2823 reduced from 2943, 2521, and 2107 respectively; all 30 issues now sit far below the 5000 cap and pass completeness validation (fetched == Jira reported total).","Marker detection operated on pre-strip rendered ADF text; 30,847 marked candidates identified; 836 unmarked comments across REB-1567, REB-1931, and REB-2605 were excluded as phase-1 non-candidates because their rendered text was truncated at 32767 chars and ended with the reconciler's own _TRUNCATION_SUFFIX, removing the trailing marker paragraph.","Rate-limiting was handled with explicit Retry-After backoff (713+ throttles absorbed, 0 failed deletions across 29,931 DELETEs); a resumability mechanism via append-only deletion log allowed recovery from interruption mid-run without data loss.","The reconcile-bridge workflow remained PAUSED throughout the operation and was not re-enabled; phase 2 (836 truncation-suffix comments) was deliberately left unexecuted for a separate operator decision and is available behind --include-truncated flag."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b2b5c498-2f67-4ae3-bafc-eca40294bec2","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787439541788414376,"uuid":"df1c909f-7dd4-450c-9419-8edda9543da2"}